<title>USA: Paul Harris stake cut by Vinik group.</title>
<headline>Paul Harris stake cut by Vinik group.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group led by former Fidelity Magellan Fund manager Jeffrey Vinik said Thursday it has reduced its stake in Paul Harris Stores Inc to 4.7 percent or 531,200 shares.</p>
<p>In a filing with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission, the group said it sold 95,000 shares of the women's clothing retailer on July 17 at $15.75 each.</p>
